* stop_on_error_regression.dts
* Proves the stop_on_error[severity] threshold.
*
* Deterministic trigger: STOP_ON_ERROR with an invalid severity records an
* error-severity canonical code through the messaging/emit path
* (e_invalid_argument), so no table fixtures are needed.
*
* Expected behavior:
*   - Phase 1 (threshold OFF): the recorded error does NOT abort; the run
*     continues and PASS-1 prints.
*   - Phase 2 (threshold ERROR): the recorded error DOES abort the run at the
*     failing line; a "stopped (STOP_ON_ERROR ERROR)" line prints and NEITHER
*     FAIL-2 NOR FAIL-3 print.
*
* Run:  DOTSCRIPT dottalkpp/data/scripts/errorstop/stop_on_error_regression.dts
*   or: dottalkpp.exe --script dottalkpp/data/scripts/errorstop/stop_on_error_regression.dts

FORMULA "STOP_ON_ERROR-REGRESSION-BEGIN"

* --- Phase 1: threshold OFF -> a recorded error must NOT abort ---
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR __BOGUS_SEVERITY__
FORMULA "PASS-1-OFF-CONTINUED-PAST-ERROR"

* --- Phase 2: threshold ERROR -> a recorded error MUST abort here ---
STOP_ON_ERROR ERROR
STOP_ON_ERROR __BOGUS_SEVERITY__
FORMULA "FAIL-2-SHOULD-NOT-PRINT-AFTER-ABORT"

* If the abort works, execution never reaches this end marker.
FORMULA "FAIL-3-END-SHOULD-NOT-PRINT"
